    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note"><strong>Privacy:</strong> you do not need to share your real birth date, appointments, or work schedule. Use invented information whenever you prefer.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A weekly schedule:</b> Say one real or invented activity for three workdays. <span class="ex">On Monday I have a team meeting. On Friday I finish early.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>An invented birthday:</b> Give a month and an exact date. <span class="ex">My birthday is on June 16th. It's in June.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Book an appointment:</b> Role-play with the teacher. <span class="ex">I'd like an appointment on Wednesday.</span> &nbsp;<span class="ex">Is March 8th okay?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A deadline:</b> Pick a real or invented deadline and say it. <span class="ex">The report is due on Thursday.</span> &nbsp;<span class="ex">The project ends in December.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>What's the date?</b> Take turns. One person asks <span class="ex">What's the date today?</span> The other answers with a full date, then asks back.</div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: book and confirm an appointment</h3>
    <p>Use this fictional March 2026 calendar. The available appointments are <span class="ex">Tuesday, March 10</span> and <span class="ex">Thursday, March 12</span>. One person offers a date. The other accepts or asks for the second date. Ask for one repetition, then read back and confirm the final day and date. Switch roles.</p>
    <p><strong>Success criteria:</strong> distinguish the weekday from the calendar date; use <span class="ex">on</span> before the exact date; put the month first; pronounce the day as an ordinal; and finish with an accurate read-back.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “I use <strong>on</strong> for ______ (a day or a date). I use <strong>in</strong> for ______ (a month or a year). I say the date with the <strong>month first</strong>, like ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say three true sentences about your week: one with <strong>on</strong> + a day, one with <strong>in</strong> + a month, and one date in American style.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can name the days and months, choose on or in, and say a date the American way.">
    <h3>Final quiz: days, months, dates</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="on" data-hint="Friday is one exact weekday." data-fix="The meeting is on Friday.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. The meeting is ___ Friday.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on">on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in">in</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="in" data-hint="August names a whole month." data-fix="My vacation is in August.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. My vacation is ___ August.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on">on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in">in</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="on" data-hint="March 8th identifies one exact date." data-fix="The deadline is on March 8th.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The deadline is ___ March 8th.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="on">on</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="in">in</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Wednesday" data-hint="Move one day forward from Tuesday." data-fix="Wednesday comes between Tuesday and Thursday.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. Which day comes between Tuesday and Thursday?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Monday">Monday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Wednesday">Wednesday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Saturday">Saturday</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="June" data-hint="July is month 7, so choose month 6." data-fix="June comes immediately before July.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Which month comes right before July?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="May">May</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="June">June</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="August">August</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="March eighth" data-hint="In common U.S. numeric order, the first number is the month; pronounce the day as an ordinal." data-fix="3/8 → March eighth in common U.S. speech.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. How do we say the date 3/8 in American style?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="March eighth">March eighth</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="August third">August third</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="March third">March third</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="My birthday is in October." data-hint="You know only a whole month, not an exact date or weekday." data-fix="My birthday is in October.">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. You know only the birth month, October. Which sentence reports exactly that information?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="My birthday is in October.">My birthday is in October.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="My birthday is on October 12th.">My birthday is on October 12th.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="My birthday is on Monday.">My birthday is on Monday.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="January" data-hint="Choose month 1, immediately before February." data-fix="January is the first month of the year.">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. Which is the first month of the year?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="January">January</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="March">March</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="December">December</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check quiz</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset quiz</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

